-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_9 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_8 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(9) / ב(8) the supervision's enterprises`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_9 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_8 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`the enterprises demanded are within the limits`).

-- The Annual Leave Law (imported), §3, against the guide's vacation. His
-- vacation is the secondary schools' calendar (6.17.2(3)), whose summer the
-- takanon's §1.25.2 sets for post-primary institutions at 7 days for each
-- month of work (imported), and the paid school recesses are the leave the
-- law asks (convention instruments.school-recess-as-annual-leave), weighed
-- in weeks (convention instruments.leave-days-measure). The enterprises may
-- take no more than 5 of the vacation days; a full year's summer less those
-- 5 is still more than §3's 28 days. The floor is met.
`the Shelach guide's summer, less the enterprise days, meets section 3 of the Annual Leave Law` MEANS
        `the enterprises demanded are within the limits` 10 5
    AND NOT `the enterprises demanded are within the limits` 10 6
    AND `weeks of summer the takanon gives for months of work` `post-primary institutions, teacher-training institutions and youth centres` 10
            MINUS (5 DIVIDED BY 7)
            AT LEAST `weeks of leave the law's days make` `most days of leave section 3 gives a year`
#ASSERT `the Shelach guide's summer, less the enterprise days, meets section 3 of the Annual Leave Law`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_10 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_7 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(10) / ב(7) pedagogical councils`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_11 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_9 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(11) / ב(9) training on probation`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_12 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_10 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(12) / ב(10) training when permanent`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_12 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_10 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`a permanent guide's training is within two weeks`).

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: "חודש ימים מראש" in 3א(13) and 3ב(11)
-- is a month's notice of a demand to instruct at a seminar; it is no notice
-- of a dismissal or a resignation.
-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_13 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_11 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(13) / ב(11) instructing at courses`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_14 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_12 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(14) / ב(12) working by the rules`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_a__subpara_15 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_b__subpara_13 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3 א(15) / ב(13) moving district`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_c as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.3ג coordinating a split position`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_c as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`the split-position guide's share of central enterprises is within bounds`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_d as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`hours in a field day`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_d as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`the month's field days are in order`).

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_e
GIVEN `days the enterprise lasts` IS A NUMBER, `held where the supervision set` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the national service enterprise is as set` `days the enterprise lasts` `held where the supervision set` IF
    `days the enterprise lasts` AT MOST 14 AND `held where the supervision set`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p1 The circumstance that motivates the next paragraphs (the supervision cannot always provide substitutes); it states no rule of its own.

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p2
GIVEN `a substitute from the guides' team` IS A BOOLEAN, `a training centre in the area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `training day place`
DECIDE `where the present guide holds the training day` `a substitute from the guides' team` `a training centre in the area` IS
    IF `a substitute from the guides' team`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a training centre in the area`
         THEN JUST `a training centre where other guides are with their classes at that time`
         ELSE JUST `near the school`

-- ¶3: in every case every possibility of holding the training day is
-- examined and its cancellation avoided. The text names no one who does it.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p3
GIVEN `every possibility of holding it was examined` IS A BOOLEAN, `no possibility of holding it remains` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the training day may be cancelled` `every possibility of holding it was examined` `no possibility of holding it remains` IF
    `every possibility of holding it was examined` AND `no possibility of holding it remains`

-- ¶4: the guide answers personally for the equipment handed to him; lost
-- or damaged by his negligence, he returns equal equipment or its value in
-- money as the supervision assesses; he may appeal by a reasoned request to
-- the coordinating supervisor, who sets up a parity committee.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p4
GIVEN `lost or damaged by the guide's negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `6.17 party` `6.17 action`
DECIDE `6.17.3ו equipment lost by negligence` `lost or damaged by the guide's negligence` IS
    IF `lost or damaged by the guide's negligence`
    THEN PARTY `the Shelach guide`
         MUST  `return equipment of equal value, or its value in money as the supervision assesses it`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the Shelach guide` BECAUSE "6.17.3ו: the guide answers personally for the equipment handed to him"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p4
GIVETH A DEONTIC `6.17 party` `6.17 action`
DECIDE `appealing the equipment assessment` IS
    PARTY `the Shelach guide`
    MAY   `appeal the equipment assessment by a reasoned request to the coordinating supervisor`
    HENCE (PARTY `the coordinating supervisor`
           MUST  `set up a parity committee to examine the matter`)

-- ¶5: the committee's decision is final; the sum is the guide's debt to the
-- government, which the Ministry may deduct from his salary and any other
-- sum the government owes him, subject to the Wage Protection Law, 1958.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p5
GIVEN `the sum the committee finally decided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the guide's debt to the government` `the sum the committee finally decided` IS
    `the sum the committee finally decided`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_3__para_f/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC `6.17 party` `6.17 action`
DECIDE `deducting the debt` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry`
    MAY   `deduct the debt from the guide's salary or from any other sum the government owes him` lawful PROVIDED lawful

-- What "בכפיפות לחוק הגנת השכר" leaves of the deduction from his salary in
-- a month (l4/laws/wage-protection-law.l4, §25): a debt under the guide's
-- written undertaking to the employer, no more than a quarter of the
-- month's wage (§25(א)(6)); from his last wage, when he stops working, the
-- whole balance (§25(ב)); without either, §25 lists no ground, and nothing
-- is deducted from his salary — the sum stays a debt the government may
-- claim otherwise. So the deduction the section allows is never more than
-- the law lets: against the Wage Protection Law (MMS-601), it meets the
-- floor.
GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER
      `the month's wage` IS A NUMBER
      `he undertook the debt in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is his last wage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the debt 6.17.3ו deducts from a month's salary` `the debt` `the month's wage` `he undertook the debt in writing` `it is his last wage` IS
    IF `it is his last wage`
    THEN `what section 25(ב) lets be deducted from the last wage` TRUE `the debt` `the month's wage`
    ELSE IF `he undertook the debt in writing`
         THEN min `the debt` (`the most section 25(א)(6) lets be deducted in a month` `the month's wage`)
         ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the debt 6.17.3ו deducts from a month's salary` 4000 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `the debt 6.17.3ו deducts from a month's salary` 4000 10000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the debt 6.17.3ו deducts from a month's salary` 4000 10000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 4000
-- The agreement's 1978 rule (its 4(יד)) deducts the same.
#ASSERT `the debt the 1978 regulations deduct from a month's salary` 4000 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the debt 6.17.3ו deducts from a month's salary` 4000 10000 TRUE FALSE

