-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_11/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_11/p2 The source (אסמכתא) of section 6.17.11.

§§ `6.17.12 העברה להוראה`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12__para_1 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.12.1 the pedagogical committee`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12__para_1 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.12.1 a guide unfit to teach`).

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12__para_2 as in the Shelah agreement of 1978, `1978-01-13_teachers_shelach-teachers-agreement` (`6.17.12.2 a guide asking to become a teacher`).

-- 3: the rights accrued since he began as a guide, seniority included, run
-- on unbroken, by the rules of אמח"י (or any instruction amending them),
-- and also where the teaching is under an owner other than the government.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12__para_3
GIVEN `moved to teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the continuity of the rights accrued as a guide, seniority included, is kept` `moved to teaching` IF
    `moved to teaching`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12/p2 The source (אסמכתא) of section 6.17.12.
-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12/p3 akn:chp_6__sec_6_17__ssec_6_17_12/p4 §6.17.6 (instruction or teaching licence) is a pointer to section 1.21.2.3 of the takanon, encoded there.

§§ `Worked examples`

#ASSERT `grade of the guide` `a matriculated certified guide` EQUALS `certified Shelach guide`
#ASSERT `grade of the guide` `a 10-year guide with Shelach, psychology and Hebrew` EQUALS `non-certified Shelach guide A`
#ASSERT `a regular guide's pay for an overnight activity` `a guide in the composed full position` 8 EQUALS 9000 DIVIDED BY 120 TIMES 6 TIMES 1.24
#ASSERT `an outside worker's pay for an overnight activity` 12000 12 EQUALS 1240
#ASSERT `pay for substituting another guide` `a guide in the composed full position` 4 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `released from` (`guide mother` WITH `is pregnant` IS FALSE, `gave birth` IS TRUE, `is a mother` IS TRUE, `child's age in years` IS 1, `is nursing, with a medical certificate` IS FALSE) EQUALS `release` WITH `physical work` IS FALSE, `treks` IS FALSE, `national service` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `entitled to tenure` `a guide in the composed full position` 2 2 TRUE

-- The full-position guide joins the IDF march: fulfilled. A guide who wants
-- to move district and applies 10 days after the end of May: breached.
#TRACE `6.17.3 א(4) the IDF march` `a guide in the composed full position` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Shelach guide` DOES `perform` `taking part in the IDF's march with the school team` AT 10
#TRACE `6.17.3 א(15) / ב(13) moving district` TRUE 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Shelach guide` DOES `perform` `applying in writing, by the end of May of that year, to move from one district of the Ministry to another` AT 70
#TRACE `paying the overnight arrears` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `pay the overnight reward for 1.9.98 to payment with January 2003's salary` AT 1
#TRACE `appealing the equipment assessment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Shelach guide` DOES `appeal the equipment assessment by a reasoned request to the coordinating supervisor` AT 3
    PARTY `the coordinating supervisor` DOES `set up a parity committee to examine the matter` AT 10

§§ `Property checks`

-- 6.17.2.2ב over every guide and report, the day before and the day of
-- 1.9.94: the surplus hours are never negative, never more than 4 or than
-- the hours reported, none before 1.9.94 or below a full position, and a
-- larger report never accumulates fewer. F-6.17-b over the same space:
-- the composed full position's 6 frontal hours of 24 never meet the third,
-- and 8 do.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN fr YIELD
                        all (GIVEN w YIELD
                                all (GIVEN r YIELD
                                        LET g MEANS `a checked guide` f fr w `certified Shelach guide`
                                            a MEANS `surplus hours accumulated this week` g r (Date 1 9 1994)
                                        IN      a AT LEAST 0
                                            AND a AT MOST 4
                                            AND a AT MOST r
                                            AND `surplus hours accumulated this week` g r (Date 31 8 1994) EQUALS 0
                                            AND (f AT LEAST 1 OR a EQUALS 0)
                                            AND `surplus hours accumulated this week` g (r PLUS 1) (Date 1 9 1994) AT LEAST a)
                                    (range 0 6))
                            (LIST 12, 24, 30))
                    (range 0 12))
            (LIST 1/2, 1, 5/4)
`the third is met from 8 frontal hours of 24, not at 6` MEANS
        (NOT `field-day preparation hours count as surplus hours for the Dafna fund` (`a checked guide` 1 6 24 `certified Shelach guide`))
    AND `field-day preparation hours count as surplus hours for the Dafna fund` (`a checked guide` 1 8 24 `certified Shelach guide`)
#ASSERT `the third is met from 8 frontal hours of 24, not at 6`

-- 6.17.3 א(5) and ה over 0 to 20 days: the two clauses set the national
-- service at the same 14 days; the supervision's enterprises keep to 10
-- days and 5 of vacation, and fewer days never break the limits; a field
-- day is 6 hours, and longer days, once approved, fill exactly the quota.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD
                    `the national service demanded is within 14 days` d EQUALS `the national service enterprise is as set` d TRUE
                AND `the national service demanded is within 14 days` d EQUALS (d AT MOST 14)
                AND all (GIVEN v YIELD
                                (NOT `the enterprises demanded are within the limits` d v)
                             OR (    d AT MOST 10
                                 AND v AT MOST 5
                                 AND `the enterprises demanded are within the limits` (max 0 (d MINUS 1)) (max 0 (v MINUS 1))))
                        (range 0 d))
            (range 0 20)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD
                    `the month's field days are in order` FALSE h 10 60 EQUALS (h EQUALS 6)
                AND `the month's field days are in order` TRUE h 5 60 EQUALS (h TIMES 5 EQUALS 60))
            (range 4 14)

GIVEN s IS A `guide schooling`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `definitions met by` s IS
    count (filter (GIVEN b YIELD b) (LIST `is a certified Shelach guide` s, `is stage AA` s, `is non-certified A` s))

GIVEN s IS A `guide schooling`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `6.17.5, for every schooling` s IF
        ((NOT `is a certified Shelach guide` s) OR `grade of the guide` s EQUALS `certified Shelach guide`)
    AND ((NOT `is stage AA` s) OR `the rank of` (`grade of the guide` s) AT LEAST 2)
    AND ((NOT `is non-certified A` s) OR `the rank of` (`grade of the guide` s) AT LEAST 1)
    AND (`definitions met by` s AT LEAST 1 OR `grade of the guide` s EQUALS `non-certified Shelach guide B`)
    AND `the rank of` (`grade of the guide` (`a checked schooling` (s's `years of schooling`) (s's `has a Hebrew matriculation certificate`) (s's `finished the Gadna guides' seminar`) (s's `passed Gadna and its teaching`) TRUE (s's `passed psychology`) (s's `passed Hebrew language`) (s's `positive supervision assessment for a year or more`) (s's `exams of the 1962 booklet still owed`) (s's `the one exam owed is Shelach and its teaching`)))
        AT LEAST `the rank of` (`grade of the guide` s)
    AND `the rank of` (`grade of the guide` (`a checked schooling` (s's `years of schooling`) (s's `has a Hebrew matriculation certificate`) (s's `finished the Gadna guides' seminar`) (s's `passed Gadna and its teaching`) (s's `passed Shelach and its teaching`) TRUE TRUE (s's `positive supervision assessment for a year or more`) (s's `exams of the 1962 booklet still owed`) (s's `the one exam owed is Shelach and its teaching`)))
        AT LEAST `the rank of` (`grade of the guide` s)
#ASSERT `holds for every schooling` `6.17.5, for every schooling`

`the grade definitions of (3) to (5) overlap` MEANS
        `a matriculated certified guide is also "non-certified A"`
    AND `is stage AA` `an 11-year guide owing Hebrew alone`
    AND `is non-certified A` `an 11-year guide owing Hebrew alone`
#ASSERT `the grade definitions of (3) to (5) overlap`

-- 6.17.7 over 0 to 14 hours worked and owed: an outside worker is paid for
-- at most 10 hours and never less for more; a regular guide's overnight
-- pay never negative and never more for more hours owed; a sortie of 24
-- hours or more pays at most 20 hours, a shorter one none; a field day is
-- no special activity; the overnight reward is nothing before 1.9.98.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD
                    `an outside worker's pay for an overnight activity` 12000 h AT MOST `an outside worker's pay for an overnight activity` 12000 10
                AND `an outside worker's pay for an overnight activity` 12000 (h PLUS 1) AT LEAST `an outside worker's pay for an overnight activity` 12000 h
                AND `a regular guide's pay for an overnight activity` `a guide in the composed full position` h AT LEAST 0
                AND `a regular guide's pay for an overnight activity` `a guide in the composed full position` (h PLUS 1)
                    AT MOST `a regular guide's pay for an overnight activity` `a guide in the composed full position` h
                AND `hours paid for a sortie` (h PLUS 10) h AT MOST 20
                AND `hours paid for a sortie` 23 h EQUALS 0
                AND `hours paid for a day activity` h 0 TRUE EQUALS 0)
            (range 0 14)
#ASSERT `overnight reward` (Date 31 8 1998) TRUE 56.84 EQUALS 0 AND `overnight reward` (Date 1 9 1998) TRUE 56.84 EQUALS 56.84

#ASSERT all (GIVEN w YIELD
                all (GIVEN o YIELD
                            (`1.2's hours as printed` w o LESS THAN 0) EQUALS (o GREATER THAN min w 10)
                        AND `hours paid for a day activity` w o FALSE EQUALS max (`1.2's hours as printed` w o) 0)
                    (range 0 10))
            (range 0 14)

`an activity of 4 hours on a day the roster owes 6 is negative as printed` MEANS
        `1.2's hours as printed` 4 6 LESS THAN 0
    AND `hours paid for a day activity` 4 6 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `an activity of 4 hours on a day the roster owes 6 is negative as printed`

-- 6.17.7 clothing over every position in quarters: never more than a full
-- position's (2 suits, a windbreaker in its year, a pair of boots), and
-- never less for a larger position.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN k YIELD
                LET f MEANS k DIVIDED BY 4
                    c MEANS `clothing for the year` (`a checked guide` f 6 24 `certified Shelach guide`) TRUE
                    d MEANS `clothing for the year` (`a checked guide` (f PLUS 1/4) 6 24 `certified Shelach guide`) TRUE
                IN      c's `suits` AT MOST 2 AND c's `windbreakers` AT MOST 1 AND c's `pairs of paratrooper boots` AT MOST 1
                    AND d's `suits` AT LEAST c's `suits`
                    AND d's `windbreakers` AT LEAST c's `windbreakers`
                    AND d's `pairs of paratrooper boots` AT LEAST c's `pairs of paratrooper boots`
                    AND (`clothing for the year` (`a checked guide` f 6 24 `certified Shelach guide`) FALSE)'s `windbreakers` EQUALS 0)
            (range 0 6)

`6.17.12.1 names no one to put the guide before the committee` MEANS
    NOT (at `the sentences of 6.17.12.1` 0)'s `names who acts`
#ASSERT `6.17.12.1 names no one to put the guide before the committee`
